> is x odd?
  note: "odd": read as an odd function, f(-x) = -f(x), not an odd number for every input (say "an odd function" or "always odd")
  ucas: it(x) = x
  ucas: parity it
parity of it:
  odd: f(-x) = -f(x)
  proved symbolically (parity rules: x is odd; sums keep a common parity, products multiply it; sin/tan/atan preserve it, cos/abs make it even)
> is x odd even?
  note: "odd": read as an odd function, f(-x) = -f(x), not an odd number for every input (say "an odd function" or "always odd")
  sorry: I didn't follow "even"
> is x even odd?
  note: "even": read as an even function, f(-x) = f(x), not an even number for every input (say "an even function" or "always even")
  sorry: I didn't follow "odd"
> the sign of x
  ucas: it(x) = sign(x)
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = sign(x)
  -> real
> the sign of the sign of x
  ucas: it(x) = sign(sign(x))
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = sign(sign(x))
  -> real
> the sign of the sign of the sign of x
  ucas: it(x) = sign(sign(sign(x)))
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = sign(sign(sign(x)))
  -> real
> the sqrt of the sqrt of x
  ucas: it(x) = sqrt(sqrt(x))
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = sqrt(sqrt(x))
  -> real
